   "title": "Korea expands benefits for retired working dogs to help them find forever homes",
   "url": "https://www.koreatimes.co.kr/southkorea/environment-animals/20261031/korea-expands-benefits-for-retired-working-dogs-to-help-them-find-forever-homes",
   "domain": "koreatimes.co.kr",
   "source": "koreatimes.co.kr",
   "published": "Sat, 31 Oct 2026 11:27:03 GMT",
   "_dt": 1793446023.0,
   "ageDays": 0.02,
   "summary": "Korea is stepping up its efforts to help retired working dogs find forever homes by building a comprehensive, state-funded safety net designed to ease the steep financial burden on adoptive families. For years, private adoption for retired working dogs faced steep hurdles. Furthermore, plans are underway to build a dedicated state retirement center to rehabilitate retired working dogs for adoption, while providing lifelong, state-funded care for senior or ill dogs that cannot be placed in private homes.",
   "summary_zh": "韩国正加大力度，帮助退役工作犬找到永久归宿。为此，韩国正在建立一套全面的国家资助安全网，以减轻收养家庭面临的经济负担。多年来，私人收养退役工作犬面临重重困难。此外，相关计划正在推进，将建设一座专门的国家退役犬中心，对退役工作犬进行康复治疗并为收养做准备，同时为无法安置在私人家庭中的老年或患病犬提供终身国家资助照护。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Korea is stepping up its efforts to help retired working dogs find forever homes by building a comprehensive, state-funded safety net designed to ease the steep financial burden on adoptive families. Under an expanded initiative led by the Ministry of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs, the government is introducing direct medical subsidies, discounted veterinary care, and dedicated hospice facilities to ensure these canine public servants are cared for after their service ends. Roughly 1,100 working dogs currently serve across six government bodies, including the military, police, fire services, customs and quarantine inspection. Among them, the Animal and Plant Quarantine Agency alone operates approximately 70 specialized detector dogs at key international travel hubs. For years, private adoption for retired working dogs faced steep hurdles. Specialized breeds like beagles, Labradors, and Malinois typically retire around age 8 after six to eight years of active duty. Upon retirement, adoptive owners are left with high medical costs for joint issues, dental problems and chronic ailments accrued during their demanding working lives. To make adoption more accessible, the ministry partnered with private veterinary groups, pet food manufacturers and insurers to slash maintenance costs. Participating clinics, which have expanded from 56 locations in 2024 to 73 in 2026, offer 30 percent discounts on treatments, while feed suppliers provide up to 50 percent off specialized nutrition. In April, the government introduced a direct subsidy program reimbursing up to 60 percent of out-of-pocket medical bills and insurance premiums, capped at 1 million won ($725) annually per dog for up to 100 retirees each year. Officials are also establishing a network of public anchor veterinary hospitals, partnering with animal hospitals at four flagship national universities — Kangwon National University, Chungbuk National University, Chungnam National University and Chonnam National University — to provide subsidized care. Furthermore, plans are underway to build a dedicated state retirement center to rehabilitate retired working dogs for adoption, while providing lifelong, state-funded care for senior or ill dogs that cannot be placed in private homes. \"We want to ensure the government honors their service with proper care and dignity,\" said Kim Jeong-wook, head of the ministry’s Agricultural Industry Innovation Policy Bureau. Organized by the ministry and the Animal and Plant Quarantine Agency, the event brought together former sniffer dogs, their handlers and their adoptive families for autumn sports and veterinary health seminars, serving as an operational review of Korea's evolving animal welfare policy. This article was published with the assistance of generative AI and edited by The Korea Times",
   "bodyLevel": "fulltext",
   "country": [
    "af"
   ],
   "topic": [
    "pol",
    "sec"
   ],
   "tier": 4,
   "actor": "第三方",
   "alsoUS": false,
   "cnHit": false,
