   "title": "921690 tinubu welcomes airtels open network launch",
   "url": "https://www.premiumtimesng.com/news/more-news/921690-tinubu-welcomes-airtels-open-network-launch.html",
   "domain": "premiumtimesng.com",
   "source": "Premium Times（尼日利亚）",
   "published": "Sat, 31 Oct 2026 07:43:33 +0000",
   "_dt": 1793432613.0,
   "ageDays": 0.17,
   "summary": "President Bola Tinubu has welcomed the launch of Airtel Nigeria’s Open Network initiative, describing it as a positive step towards greater transparency, consumer protection and improved telecommunications services in Nigeria. President Tinubu said the initiative aligns with his administration’s commitment to encouraging private-sector investment, expanding digital infrastructure, and ensuring Nigerians benefit from more reliable and accessible telecommunications services.",
   "summary_zh": "总统博拉·蒂努布欢迎Airtel Nigeria启动“开放网络”计划，称这是迈向提高透明度、保护消费者权益和改善尼日利亚电信服务的一项积极举措。蒂努布总统表示，该计划契合其政府鼓励私营部门投资、扩大数字基础设施，并确保尼日利亚民众享受到更加可靠和便捷电信服务的承诺。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "President Bola Tinubu has welcomed the launch of Airtel Nigeria’s Open Network initiative, describing it as a positive step towards greater transparency, consumer protection and improved telecommunications services in Nigeria. President Tinubu said the initiative aligns with his administration’s commitment to encouraging private-sector investment, expanding digital infrastructure, and ensuring Nigerians benefit from more reliable and accessible telecommunications services. He welcomed the growing emphasis on transparency in the sector, including the NCC’s public network coverage maps, performance information and consumer satisfaction surveys, which help Nigerians better understand the services available to them and hold operators accountable. The president also highlighted the federal government’s recent Zero-Rated Access to Educational Platforms and Content Initiative, implemented through the NCC in collaboration with the Federal Ministry of Education and telecommunications operators. The programme, designed to provide eligible students with up to 100MB of free daily data to access approved educational websites and learning resources, reflects his administration’s determination to make digital opportunities more accessible, particularly to young Nigerians. He welcomed Airtel Nigeria’s continued investment in network expansion, which has seen its infrastructure grow from approximately 15,000 sites two years ago to more than 17,000 nationwide. The expansion includes more than 1,050 network sites added during the company’s 2025/26 financial year, including 657 5G sites. President Tinubu said sustained investment in telecommunications infrastructure is essential to expanding broadband access, improving network capacity, and supporting businesses, education, and economic opportunities across Nigeria. He commended the NCC, under the leadership of Dr Maida, for its continued efforts to strengthen regulatory oversight, promote transparency and protect telecommunications consumers. The president urged operators to sustain investment in network expansion, particularly in underserved communities, and ensure that customer complaints receive timely attention. He emphasised that the success of telecommunications investment and innovation must ultimately be measured by the experience of Nigerians who depend on these services for their livelihoods, businesses and everyday communication. President Tinubu reaffirmed his administration’s commitment to maintaining a business environment that encourages responsible investment and innovation while ensuring that consumer interests remain central to telecommunications development. He called on operators to translate their investments into better network coverage, fewer service disruptions and more responsive customer service for Nigerians",
   "bodyLevel": "fulltext",
