   "title": "Excessive cutting of support columns blamed for deadly Ulsan power plant collapse",
   "url": "https://www.koreatimes.co.kr/southkorea/20261030/excessive-cutting-of-support-columns-blamed-for-deadly-ulsan-power-plant-collapse",
   "domain": "koreatimes.co.kr",
   "source": "koreatimes.co.kr",
   "published": "Fri, 30 Oct 2026 05:42:03 GMT",
   "_dt": 1793338923.0,
   "ageDays": 1.25,
   "summary": "The deadly collapse of a boiler tower at a power plant in Ulsan last November was caused by excessive cutting of support columns ahead of its planned demolition by explosives, according to a probe result released Friday. The Ministry of Land, Infrastructure and Transport released the findings of an investigation committee into the deadly accident at the Ulsan Thermal Power Plant, about 300 kilometers southeast of Seoul.",
   "summary_zh": "周五公布的调查结果显示，去年11月蔚山一座发电厂发生的致命锅炉塔倒塌事故，是由于在原定使用炸药拆除前过度切割支撑柱所致。国土交通部公布了调查委员会对蔚山热电厂致命事故的调查结果。该厂位于首尔东南约300公里处。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "The deadly collapse of a boiler tower at a power plant in Ulsan last November was caused by excessive cutting of support columns ahead of its planned demolition by explosives, according to a probe result released Friday. The Ministry of Land, Infrastructure and Transport released the findings of an investigation committee into the deadly accident at the Ulsan Thermal Power Plant, about 300 kilometers southeast of Seoul. A 63.4-meter-tall boiler tower at Unit 5 of the plant collapsed during preparations for demolition, killing seven workers and injuring two others. Investigators found that too many support columns had been cut due to flawed structural assessments, leaving them unable to support the weight of the upper structure. To prevent similar accidents, the committee suggested stricter on-site inspections, new technical standards for demolition work and tighter oversight of high-risk demolition projects",
   "bodyLevel": "fulltext",
   "country": [
    "kr"
   ],
