   "title": "US sanctions N. Korean network accused of defrauding businesses",
   "url": "https://www.koreatimes.co.kr/world/20261029/us-sanctions-n-korean-network-accused-of-defrauding-businesses",
   "domain": "koreatimes.co.kr",
   "source": "koreatimes.co.kr",
   "published": "Thu, 29 Oct 2026 02:42:03 GMT",
   "_dt": 1793241723.0,
   "ageDays": 2.38,
   "summary": "The United States imposed sanctions on Wednesday to target what the Treasury Department said were North Korean government-run schemes that use IT workers to defraud U.S. businesses and generate revenue for Pyongyang's weapons programs. The Treasury Department said the schemes involve North Korean IT workers fraudulently gaining employment with companies in the United States and elsewhere, and Pyongyang taking most of the workers' wages to fund its weapons of mass destruction and ballistic missile programs.",
   "summary_zh": "美国于周三实施制裁，以打击美国财政部所称由朝鲜政府掌控、利用信息技术人员诈骗美国企业并为平壤武器计划创造收入的阴谋。财政部称，这些阴谋涉及朝鲜信息技术人员通过欺诈手段在 美国及其他地区的公司获得就业，随后平壤拿走这些人员的大部分工资，为其大规模杀伤性武器和弹道导弹计划提供资金。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "The United States imposed sanctions on Wednesday to target what the Treasury Department said were North Korean government-run schemes that use IT workers to defraud U.S. businesses and generate revenue for Pyongyang's weapons programs. The Treasury Department said the schemes involve North Korean IT workers fraudulently gaining employment with companies in the United States and elsewhere, and Pyongyang taking most of the workers' wages to fund its weapons of mass destruction and ballistic missile programs. \"These networks permeate through the global financial system, necessitating a unified response to match the threat,\" the department said in a statement, adding that Australia and the European Union also imposed North Korea-related sanctions this month. North Korea's mission to the United Nations in New York did not immediately respond to a request for comment. The sanctions come as U.S. President Donald Trump has been eager to jump-start talks with North Korea, but Pyongyang has shown little interest in diplomacy aimed at containing its nuclear program. However, earlier this month Trump downplayed the idea of another high-profile meeting with Kim in China next month. Trump became the only U.S. president to have met a North Korean leader when he held an unprecedented series of summits with Kim in 2018 and 2019, but the diplomatic efforts broke down over U.S. demands that North Korea give up its nuclear weapons. Trump has since referred to North Korea repeatedly as a \"nuclear power,\" although his administration has continued to call for the country's denuclearization and has not formally recognized it as a nuclear-weapons state. The Treasury Department sanctioned a separate North Korean IT worker network in March",
