   "platform": "x",
   "title": "Unilateral sanctions don't work.",
   "url": "https://x.com/TiMuzira/status/2116202467927203875",
   "snippet": "Unilateral sanctions don't work. History proves that one-sided economic pressure fails to force a strategic retreat when a state views its security as a vital priority.\n\nLook at what happened in the Sahel—years of U.S. sanctions targeting Mali's defense officials completely failed to change their strategy, ultimately forcing Washington to quietly lift them to salvage regional operations. Applying this pressure unevenly reveals a glaring double standard: penalizing Rwanda’s defense structures - which will not work - while giving the DRC preferential treatment, despite Kinshasa harboring extremist negative forces like the FDLR on its soil.\n\nTrue stability requires balanced diplomacy and addressing all security threats, not blunt isolation.",
   "body": "Unilateral sanctions don't work. History proves that one-sided economic pressure fails to force a strategic retreat when a state views its security as a vital priority.\n\nLook at what happened in the Sahel—years of U.S. sanctions targeting Mali's defense officials completely failed to change their strategy, ultimately forcing Washington to quietly lift them to salvage regional operations. Applying this pressure unevenly reveals a glaring double standard: penalizing Rwanda’s defense structures - which will not work - while giving the DRC preferential treatment, despite Kinshasa harboring extremist negative forces like the FDLR on its soil.\n\nTrue stability requires balanced diplomacy and addressing all security threats, not blunt isolation.",
